        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While campaigning the week before the midterms, health secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. visited Sheepgate, a Christian addiction recovery center in Colfax, Iowa. Sheepgate, Kennedy said, is a model for the type of faith-based center that doesn&#x2019;t receive federal funding but that he believes should.&#xa0;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#x201c;We took a wonderful tour today and it was really impressive and really touching,&#x201d; Kennedy said in a <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7524115191417159680/\">video</a> about the <a href=\"https://iowacapitaldispatch.com/2026/10/28/hhs-secretary-robert-f-kennedy-jr-says-feds-looking-for-ways-to-fund-faith-based-recovery-programs/\">visit</a>.&#xa0;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/17/rfk-jr-federal-funding-faith-based-recovery-groups/?utm_campaign=rss\">Read the rest&hellip;</a></p>"
      }
